00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:14,740
(Watch on KonFlix.vip)

1
00:02:01,505 --> 00:02:02,625
Hang in there.

2
00:02:03,825 --> 00:02:05,945
I know it hurts. Hang in there.

3
00:02:10,105 --> 00:02:12,665
Come on. I'll untie you.

4
00:02:17,305 --> 00:02:18,145
Does it hurt?

5
00:02:21,065 --> 00:02:22,425
Those traffickers should rot in hell!

6
00:02:22,505 --> 00:02:23,345
They should rot!

7
00:02:23,425 --> 00:02:25,065
<i>They all deserve it! They all do!</i>

8
00:02:26,705 --> 00:02:27,545
<i>That kid.</i>

9
00:02:27,625 --> 00:02:29,105
Why did he go to your place after?

10
00:02:31,425 --> 00:02:33,465
Pony, he told me

11
00:02:33,545 --> 00:02:35,505
his parents always fought.

12
00:02:36,225 --> 00:02:38,545
He didn't want to go home.

13
00:02:39,665 --> 00:02:43,145
He asked me if I could take him in.

14
00:03:04,145 --> 00:03:06,945
Come on. Have a bit more.

15
00:03:09,545 --> 00:03:10,625
Thanks, Daddy Peng.

16
00:03:20,105 --> 00:03:21,105
Pony.

17
00:03:27,105 --> 00:03:28,625
Eat up. Here.

18
00:03:40,625 --> 00:03:43,545
-Thanks, Daddy Peng.
-You're welcome.

19
00:03:52,545 --> 00:03:55,225
<i>CHINESE HISTORY, GRADE 8 VOL.2</i>

20
00:04:11,985 --> 00:04:13,025
Daddy Peng.

21
00:04:13,745 --> 00:04:15,225
I'm going back to school today.

22
00:04:15,305 --> 00:04:18,225
Okay. Then after school, I'll pick you up.

23
00:04:18,305 --> 00:04:19,105
No need.

24
00:04:19,184 --> 00:04:20,825
I haven't been home for days.

25
00:04:20,905 --> 00:04:22,265
My parents must be worried.

26
00:04:26,545 --> 00:04:27,865
I won't come here anymore.

27
00:04:27,945 --> 00:04:30,665
Daddy Peng, thanks for taking care of me.

28
00:04:47,425 --> 00:04:48,545
Dad's here.

29
00:04:49,545 --> 00:04:50,665
This is your home.

30
00:04:50,745 --> 00:04:51,785
From now on,

31
00:04:51,865 --> 00:04:54,265
focus on your studies
and keep up with your homework.

32
00:04:56,185 --> 00:04:58,945
As for school,
you don't need to go anymore.

33
00:05:00,185 --> 00:05:01,785
This is your home.

34
00:05:02,545 --> 00:05:03,945
I'll teach you at home.

35
00:05:05,785 --> 00:05:07,945
Pony is too young. He doesn't understand.

36
00:05:08,465 --> 00:05:11,145
He has no idea how I feel as his dad.

37
00:05:11,225 --> 00:05:14,825
What I fear most is that
he'll run away again someday.

38
00:05:15,785 --> 00:05:16,705
Then what am I supposed to do?

39
00:05:16,785 --> 00:05:18,385
What am I supposed to do?

40
00:05:19,345 --> 00:05:21,585
That's why I need to keep more ponies.

41
00:05:21,665 --> 00:05:23,265
So I can feel at ease.

42
00:05:42,185 --> 00:05:43,025
Going to an internet cafe?

43
00:05:43,945 --> 00:05:44,985
I'll give you a ride.

44
00:05:48,945 --> 00:05:50,385
No charge. Get in.

45
00:05:52,025 --> 00:05:52,945
Thanks, sir.

46
00:05:59,665 --> 00:06:00,625
Eat.

47
00:06:02,345 --> 00:06:04,585
Do you want to stay over tonight?

48
00:06:05,185 --> 00:06:05,985
Huh?

49
00:06:06,065 --> 00:06:08,225
I run a Trojan Horse Hotel here.
It's upstairs.

50
00:06:08,305 --> 00:06:10,545
I… I don't have money.

51
00:06:10,625 --> 00:06:13,545
No need to pay. Free.

52
00:06:14,225 --> 00:06:15,665
It's convenient
both upstairs and downstairs.

53
00:06:15,745 --> 00:06:17,905
Everything's right here.
Do whatever you like.

54
00:06:17,985 --> 00:06:19,105
Sounds good.

55
00:06:19,185 --> 00:06:20,305
Sounds good.

56
00:06:20,385 --> 00:06:22,305
-That's nice!
-Nice!

57
00:06:22,385 --> 00:06:23,225
Eat.

58
00:06:24,825 --> 00:06:26,145
One pony.

59
00:06:27,585 --> 00:06:28,585
Two ponies.

60
00:06:29,505 --> 00:06:30,945
Three ponies.

61
00:06:31,625 --> 00:06:33,185
Four ponies.

62
00:06:34,705 --> 00:06:36,345
I have four ponies.

63
00:06:37,025 --> 00:06:38,945
I cook for them every day.

64
00:06:39,025 --> 00:06:41,585
<i>I study with them</i>
<i>and teach them how to behave.</i>

65
00:06:43,345 --> 00:06:44,745
What about Han Zi'ang?

66
00:06:44,825 --> 00:06:45,865
What's wrong with him?

67
00:06:53,425 --> 00:06:54,985
This pony is too disobedient.

68
00:06:55,625 --> 00:06:57,825
Too disobedient. Too disobedient!

69
00:06:59,225 --> 00:07:00,505
Too disobedient.

70
00:07:05,025 --> 00:07:07,065
You must be starving. Eat up.

71
00:07:08,145 --> 00:07:09,305
Thanks, sir.

72
00:07:09,945 --> 00:07:10,985
My mom already cooked.

73
00:07:11,065 --> 00:07:12,185
She's waiting at home.

74
00:07:46,545 --> 00:07:48,385
Help! Help!

75
00:08:56,145 --> 00:08:58,265
YUANLONGLI INTERNATIONAL GARDEN

76
00:08:58,345 --> 00:08:59,545
You're back?

77
00:09:00,385 --> 00:09:01,225
You're back.

78
00:09:01,905 --> 00:09:04,105
Peng is weird. Why's he ignoring me?

79
00:09:04,185 --> 00:09:05,505
-Right.
-No idea.

80
00:09:13,745 --> 00:09:16,865
"If life deceives you…"

81
00:09:17,545 --> 00:09:20,745
"If life deceives you…"

82
00:09:21,945 --> 00:09:25,665
"…don't be sad, don't be anxious."

83
00:09:26,265 --> 00:09:29,625
"…don't be sad, don't be anxious."

84
00:09:29,705 --> 00:09:31,025
"Believe it,

85
00:09:31,105 --> 00:09:32,425
-the happy days…"
-Daddy Peng,

86
00:09:34,065 --> 00:09:35,305
I need the bathroom.

87
00:09:42,225 --> 00:09:43,505
Go ahead.

88
00:09:48,385 --> 00:09:49,785
Come on. Let's continue.

89
00:09:50,825 --> 00:09:54,145
"The heart always longs for the future."

90
00:09:54,745 --> 00:09:57,705
"The heart always longs for the future."

91
00:09:57,785 --> 00:10:01,105
"Now is often full of sorrow."

92
00:10:11,945 --> 00:10:14,585
Pony, where's the bathroom?

93
00:10:17,625 --> 00:10:19,065
Let go of me! You bad guy!

94
00:10:22,865 --> 00:10:25,345
You bit me! How dare you bite me!

95
00:10:26,065 --> 00:10:27,785
That's for biting me! Try that again!

96
00:10:28,665 --> 00:10:29,785
I swear I'll kill you.

97
00:10:31,865 --> 00:10:33,345
You never listen. Serves you right.

98
00:10:38,385 --> 00:10:39,225
Dad…

99
00:10:40,385 --> 00:10:41,225
Dad…

100
00:10:42,025 --> 00:10:43,705
-Dad…
-Pony?

101
00:10:56,385 --> 00:10:59,465
Pony? You're back!

102
00:11:06,345 --> 00:11:07,945
Pony!

103
00:11:11,545 --> 00:11:14,545
I missed you!

104
00:11:15,585 --> 00:11:18,305
I missed you!

105
00:11:22,825 --> 00:11:25,625
My pony!

106
00:11:35,585 --> 00:11:36,425
Good work.

107
00:11:37,425 --> 00:11:39,225
Leave the rest to us.

108
00:12:01,865 --> 00:12:03,105
I've been looking for you everywhere.

109
00:12:03,185 --> 00:12:04,665
How'd you end up here?

110
00:12:04,745 --> 00:12:07,585
Listen, you did a great job today.

111
00:12:07,665 --> 00:12:09,585
Director Zou just called.

112
00:12:09,665 --> 00:12:12,585
He said he'll be highlighting

113
00:12:12,665 --> 00:12:15,785
He Xiaohe at the case briefing.

114
00:12:15,865 --> 00:12:18,185
He also granted our task force
three days off.

115
00:12:21,185 --> 00:12:23,345
What's wrong?

116
00:12:25,425 --> 00:12:26,385
Something on your mind?

117
00:12:28,345 --> 00:12:31,505
Peng Dachuang may be alive,

118
00:12:34,025 --> 00:12:37,425
but he never really
made it out of that fire.

119
00:12:39,105 --> 00:12:42,465
He tried everything
to make it up to his son.

120
00:12:43,425 --> 00:12:45,145
He's completely consumed by it.

121
00:12:52,385 --> 00:12:54,905
I remember Captain Ran mentioned
a theory in his book.

122
00:12:55,625 --> 00:12:57,025
It's called "the domino effect".

123
00:12:57,105 --> 00:13:02,065
In this case,
a lot of seemingly unrelated events

124
00:13:02,145 --> 00:13:05,785
are actually like dominoes
spaced far apart.

125
00:13:05,865 --> 00:13:09,585
Maybe the first domino to fall

126
00:13:09,665 --> 00:13:11,585
was Peng Dachuang's son.

127
00:13:16,185 --> 00:13:19,545
Family is… a strange thing.

128
00:13:20,505 --> 00:13:23,825
When everything's fine,
people start looking for trouble,

129
00:13:24,745 --> 00:13:26,105
like they have to break it somehow.

130
00:13:28,945 --> 00:13:31,785
But if it's missing a piece,

131
00:13:34,705 --> 00:13:36,825
people try hard to fix it.

132
00:13:44,385 --> 00:13:46,785
I never thought I'd become a cop.

133
00:13:49,905 --> 00:13:51,065
But when Uncle Ran was gone,

134
00:13:52,865 --> 00:13:54,145
my family felt incomplete.

135
00:13:56,225 --> 00:13:57,425
I wanted to fix it.

136
00:14:03,825 --> 00:14:05,865
Among all these lit windows,

137
00:14:08,425 --> 00:14:11,145
if one belonged to Uncle Ran,

138
00:14:13,905 --> 00:14:15,105
that'd be nice.

139
00:14:33,145 --> 00:14:34,225
SONG QINGSONG, DUE TO COLLUSION
BETWEEN WU SHANLONG AND ZHAO HONGMEI

140
00:14:34,305 --> 00:14:35,385
WROTE A RANSOM LETTER IN XU MENG'S NAME

141
00:14:35,465 --> 00:14:36,545
FURTHER USING XU MENG'S DEATH

142
00:14:36,625 --> 00:14:38,865
AND THE LEAKED DONGSHAN MINE BID
TO FORCE SONG QINGSONG OUT OF WEIYANG

143
00:14:39,905 --> 00:14:41,145
<i>After the Mount Wu accident,</i>

144
00:14:41,745 --> 00:14:43,785
<i>Xu Meng, to pay</i>
<i>for her father's treatment,</i>

145
00:14:43,865 --> 00:14:46,905
<i>went to Yuanlongli and worked</i>
<i>at Pattia as a masseuse.</i>

146
00:14:46,985 --> 00:14:50,465
<i>That decision was like the first domino</i>

147
00:14:50,545 --> 00:14:52,425
<i>in a long chain to fall,</i>

148
00:14:52,505 --> 00:14:54,705
<i>setting off a chain reaction.</i>

149
00:15:18,945 --> 00:15:19,985
Had a nightmare?

150
00:15:21,305 --> 00:15:22,385
What time is it?

151
00:15:25,865 --> 00:15:27,945
-Is the report done yet?
-Almost done.

152
00:15:30,585 --> 00:15:32,865
Perfect. Take a look
and give me your thoughts.

153
00:15:34,185 --> 00:15:36,785
I'm not used to this. Print it out later.

154
00:15:39,665 --> 00:15:43,265
Sir, we've gone paperless
at the bureau now,

155
00:15:43,345 --> 00:15:45,625
and there's a new
office automation system too.

156
00:15:45,705 --> 00:15:47,305
I got you an account set up.

157
00:15:47,385 --> 00:15:49,505
The username is your full name in pinyin,

158
00:15:49,585 --> 00:15:51,945
-and the password is…
-What system or whatever,

159
00:15:52,545 --> 00:15:53,585
I don't get it.

160
00:15:54,305 --> 00:15:58,385
Me and this computer
just don't get each other.

161
00:15:59,185 --> 00:16:00,305
Whoever wants it can use it.

162
00:16:10,385 --> 00:16:11,905
THE JUNE 30TH CASE HAS MULTIPLE SUSPECTS
AND TANGLED LEADS…

163
00:16:16,585 --> 00:16:20,465
With Song Qingsong's jump,
the June 30th case has to be closed.

164
00:16:21,345 --> 00:16:24,065
I never thought my first case

165
00:16:24,585 --> 00:16:26,585
would end like this with a full stop.

166
00:16:27,265 --> 00:16:28,745
At best, it's just a pause.

167
00:16:29,265 --> 00:16:31,705
As for Xu Meng, her body's still missing.

168
00:16:35,585 --> 00:16:39,465
Maybe one day,
her remains will surface again.

169
00:16:40,945 --> 00:16:43,265
When that happens,
don't you start crying again.

170
00:16:46,825 --> 00:16:47,665
Sir,

171
00:16:48,785 --> 00:16:50,865
if it weren't for you
scolding me back then,

172
00:16:50,945 --> 00:16:53,345
I'd probably be a teacher now.

173
00:16:53,425 --> 00:16:55,305
Good that you know.

174
00:17:03,585 --> 00:17:04,745
By the way, sir,

175
00:17:04,825 --> 00:17:06,265
I've already filed a request

176
00:17:06,345 --> 00:17:08,745
to transfer you
to the administrative department.

177
00:17:13,704 --> 00:17:14,825
It's a new department,

178
00:17:14,905 --> 00:17:18,145
not much workload, so you can spend
more time with Xiaohe.

179
00:17:25,065 --> 00:17:25,905
Sounds good.

180
00:17:29,865 --> 00:17:33,105
This little troublemaker
used to skip class every day.

181
00:17:33,825 --> 00:17:36,705
Winter break's coming.
Might as well help her with her studies.

182
00:17:39,145 --> 00:17:40,025
Sounds good.

183
00:17:41,305 --> 00:17:43,665
Let's go. Let's grab some rice noodles.

184
00:17:45,225 --> 00:17:48,105
I haven't finished the report.
Why don't you rest a bit longer?

185
00:17:48,185 --> 00:17:50,225
You want me to keep
having nightmares, right?

186
00:17:50,305 --> 00:17:52,425
-Let's go.
-Coming.

187
00:17:56,385 --> 00:17:58,185
Let me remind you,

188
00:17:58,265 --> 00:18:00,465
don't just focus on work.

189
00:18:00,545 --> 00:18:03,145
You need to think
about your personal life too.

190
00:18:04,185 --> 00:18:05,545
I'm not in a rush.

191
00:18:05,625 --> 00:18:06,945
You're not, but I am.

192
00:18:07,025 --> 00:18:10,025
You two, not one of you
gives me peace of mind.

193
00:18:10,105 --> 00:18:12,185
How am I not giving you peace of mind?

194
00:18:14,745 --> 00:18:16,625
<i>Let me introduce myself</i>

195
00:18:17,345 --> 00:18:20,505
<i>They call me a beggar…</i>

196
00:18:21,625 --> 00:18:25,785
<i>A flood took both my parents</i>

197
00:18:25,865 --> 00:18:29,625
<i>Now I live all alone</i>

198
00:18:30,825 --> 00:18:35,025
<i>With a worn-out begging basket</i>

199
00:18:35,105 --> 00:18:38,625
<i>And a bamboo stick to fend off dogs</i>

200
00:18:39,305 --> 00:18:44,185
<i>I wander through streets and alleys</i>

201
00:18:44,265 --> 00:18:46,985
<i>Past butcher stalls</i>

202
00:18:47,065 --> 00:18:48,785
<i>And restaurants</i>

203
00:18:49,305 --> 00:18:53,385
<i>Pawnshops and bank counters</i>

204
00:18:53,465 --> 00:18:57,665
<i>Calling out to ladies and gentlemen</i>

205
00:18:57,745 --> 00:19:00,345
<i>Have pity on this poor beggar…</i>

206
00:19:00,425 --> 00:19:04,665
Young little girl, no spirit,

207
00:19:05,305 --> 00:19:07,665
can't even match an old man.

208
00:19:09,825 --> 00:19:12,025
Don't lie there. Come eat
the celebratory noodles.

209
00:19:13,985 --> 00:19:15,985
Just noodles for a celebration?

210
00:19:16,065 --> 00:19:17,625
Not even a bit of oil?

211
00:19:17,705 --> 00:19:19,025
So what?

212
00:19:19,545 --> 00:19:22,825
Back then, your Uncle Ran and I
celebrated with noodles too.

213
00:19:24,105 --> 00:19:25,425
Hurry up. Come here.

214
00:19:36,545 --> 00:19:39,545
What are you looking at?
Do I have oil on my face?

215
00:19:40,585 --> 00:19:45,185
Dad, have you seen Uncle Ran again lately?

216
00:19:46,465 --> 00:19:47,905
What do you mean?

217
00:19:47,985 --> 00:19:50,145
You want me to do therapy again?

218
00:19:50,225 --> 00:19:52,905
Drop that idea.

219
00:19:52,985 --> 00:19:53,905
I'm telling you,

220
00:19:54,625 --> 00:19:58,065
right now, I'm positive and healthy,

221
00:19:58,145 --> 00:19:59,665
better than you young people.

222
00:20:00,545 --> 00:20:01,625
Hurry up. The noodles are getting cold.

223
00:20:01,705 --> 00:20:02,665
Come on.

224
00:20:05,385 --> 00:20:06,425
Eat.

225
00:20:18,825 --> 00:20:20,825
Everything in here belonged to Uncle Ran.

226
00:20:21,945 --> 00:20:24,865
You weren't really yourself before,
but now that you're better,

227
00:20:25,585 --> 00:20:28,105
I can finally
give these things back to you.

228
00:20:30,265 --> 00:20:32,545
Here, Comrade He Yuanhang.

229
00:21:13,065 --> 00:21:16,345
RETURNED MAIL: NO SUCH PERSON AT ADDRESS

230
00:21:16,425 --> 00:21:18,505
When you retired two years ago,

231
00:21:18,585 --> 00:21:20,225
you sent out all these letters.

232
00:21:21,265 --> 00:21:24,345
But they were all returned.

233
00:21:25,225 --> 00:21:27,625
Later, I checked with the registry.

234
00:21:29,465 --> 00:21:32,905
They said Uncle Ran's grandma
passed away in 1992.

235
00:21:44,065 --> 00:21:46,065
MAIL TO GRANDMA IN SHANDONG

236
00:21:46,145 --> 00:21:48,105
FROM WEIYANG, SICHUAN

237
00:21:50,825 --> 00:21:53,025
MAIL TO GRANDMA IN SHANDONG

238
00:21:53,105 --> 00:21:54,225
FROM WEIYANG, SICHUAN

239
00:21:54,305 --> 00:21:55,425
I didn't expect that all those years…

240
00:21:55,505 --> 00:21:56,865
MAIL TO GRANDMA

241
00:21:56,945 --> 00:22:00,905
…Uncle Ran had been writing letters
to his late grandma.

242
00:22:06,065 --> 00:22:07,105
This guy

243
00:22:08,625 --> 00:22:10,505
carries too many people in his heart.

244
00:22:12,145 --> 00:22:15,745
The living and the gone.

245
00:22:23,745 --> 00:22:26,865
How come I have no memory of any of this?

246
00:22:33,865 --> 00:22:34,905
It was that day.

247
00:22:34,985 --> 00:22:35,825
JUNE 3RD, 2013

248
00:22:35,905 --> 00:22:37,145
You suddenly fainted.

249
00:22:38,585 --> 00:22:39,425
After you woke up,

250
00:22:39,505 --> 00:22:42,105
you kept saying Uncle Ran
had come back from Beijing.

251
00:22:42,985 --> 00:22:44,345
I was terrified.

252
00:22:44,425 --> 00:22:46,585
I was afraid these things
would trigger you again.

253
00:22:46,665 --> 00:22:47,705
CHINA POST, SIGNATURE HE YUANHANG

254
00:22:47,785 --> 00:22:49,745
So I hid them all.

255
00:23:12,785 --> 00:23:16,705
This, is there a way
to recover the data inside?

256
00:23:17,985 --> 00:23:18,825
What for?

257
00:23:19,785 --> 00:23:22,065
I want to see if there's anyone left

258
00:23:22,145 --> 00:23:23,945
in your Uncle Ran's hometown
we can contact,

259
00:23:26,345 --> 00:23:28,545
so we can send his belongings back.

260
00:23:28,625 --> 00:23:31,825
So he can finally rest where he belongs.

261
00:23:34,985 --> 00:23:38,465
This thing is so old,
and it's been burned.

262
00:23:40,545 --> 00:23:43,265
Unless… there's some tech genius.

263
00:23:53,585 --> 00:23:58,385
I made you the property manager
to work with me.

264
00:23:58,465 --> 00:23:59,305
And what did you do?

265
00:23:59,385 --> 00:24:01,945
You're in league with those holdouts.

266
00:24:02,945 --> 00:24:04,185
If I don't pull out the big guns,

267
00:24:04,265 --> 00:24:05,825
how are we tearing
this building down next month?

268
00:24:05,905 --> 00:24:06,745
No…

269
00:24:08,345 --> 00:24:09,785
-Officer He?
-Uncle He.

270
00:24:15,065 --> 00:24:17,825
Qian Dajun, what are you up to this time?

271
00:24:18,705 --> 00:24:19,545
Come on.

272
00:24:19,625 --> 00:24:23,865
I'm wholeheartedly thinking
about the community.

273
00:24:25,025 --> 00:24:27,305
What you're saying,
the ghosts here might buy that.

274
00:24:27,385 --> 00:24:28,345
I don't.

275
00:24:30,785 --> 00:24:33,865
NEW YORK BLOCK

276
00:24:33,945 --> 00:24:36,145
Flank him from your side!

277
00:24:36,225 --> 00:24:38,345
I'll ambush him! I see him.

278
00:24:38,865 --> 00:24:39,905
Lure him over!

279
00:24:42,945 --> 00:24:46,305
Uncle He, try another way to say hi.

280
00:24:46,385 --> 00:24:47,665
You nearly scared me to death.

281
00:24:47,745 --> 00:24:50,705
If you keep staying up,
you'll be the one dropping dead.

282
00:24:53,425 --> 00:24:54,705
Take a look at this.

283
00:24:54,785 --> 00:24:58,145
Is there a way to get
the contacts from this phone?

284
00:24:59,945 --> 00:25:03,185
Uncle He, why did you bring
this burnt brick back to me again?

285
00:25:03,265 --> 00:25:05,145
Didn't I already extract it for you
two years ago?

286
00:25:05,745 --> 00:25:07,185
Two years ago?

287
00:25:08,185 --> 00:25:11,585
Two years ago, I worked my tail off.

288
00:25:13,145 --> 00:25:14,865
Why don't I remember any of it?

289
00:25:16,265 --> 00:25:18,025
Forget it. Do it for me again.

290
00:25:18,105 --> 00:25:19,145
No chance.

291
00:25:19,225 --> 00:25:22,985
This thing, once the data was extracted,
the motherboard was fried.

292
00:25:25,105 --> 00:25:26,505
Didn't I email it to you?

293
00:25:26,585 --> 00:25:29,545
All the data is in the attachments.

294
00:25:30,305 --> 00:25:31,465
I don't really get this.

295
00:25:31,545 --> 00:25:33,425
So you emailed me.

296
00:25:33,505 --> 00:25:35,705
Then, the stuff inside,
you didn't keep a copy?

297
00:25:36,865 --> 00:25:39,465
When I work, I leave no evidence.

298
00:25:42,705 --> 00:25:45,545
Uncle He, what email did you use then?

299
00:25:48,265 --> 00:25:49,585
I think…

300
00:25:50,265 --> 00:25:54,185
I think it had an eye icon.

301
00:25:54,265 --> 00:25:55,305
An eye?

302
00:26:00,145 --> 00:26:01,145
Is this it?

303
00:26:01,225 --> 00:26:03,225
Yes! That's it.

304
00:26:03,905 --> 00:26:05,665
The username is my phone number.

305
00:26:06,265 --> 00:26:07,745
The password…

306
00:26:08,865 --> 00:26:09,905
The password…

307
00:26:11,225 --> 00:26:12,505
I forgot it.

308
00:26:13,265 --> 00:26:14,545
No problem.

309
00:26:14,625 --> 00:26:17,025
I've got this. Three seconds.

310
00:26:18,985 --> 00:26:21,585
One. Two. Three.

311
00:26:22,825 --> 00:26:24,905
Who cut my power?

312
00:26:24,985 --> 00:26:28,345
Who else could it be?
That heartless creep.

313
00:26:28,425 --> 00:26:30,185
Qian Dajun!

314
00:26:30,265 --> 00:26:31,905
It must be you!

315
00:26:49,665 --> 00:26:50,545
Slow down.

316
00:26:51,425 --> 00:26:52,545
Easy.

317
00:27:03,305 --> 00:27:05,345
WEIYANG PUBLIC SECURITY BUREAU
NANSHAN BRANCH, YUANLONGLI JUNE 30TH CASE

318
00:27:08,385 --> 00:27:11,545
CRIMINAL INVESTIGATION FILES

319
00:27:16,985 --> 00:27:18,145
INTERVIEW RECORD

320
00:27:18,225 --> 00:27:20,745
YUANLONGLI JUNE 30TH CASE, SUMMARY REPORT

321
00:27:25,385 --> 00:27:26,785
What's wrong?

322
00:27:26,865 --> 00:27:28,345
The names are reversed.

323
00:27:28,425 --> 00:27:29,945
No need.

324
00:27:30,705 --> 00:27:33,385
He, we need to stick to the facts.

325
00:27:33,465 --> 00:27:34,505
I'm sticking to the facts.

326
00:27:35,865 --> 00:27:38,025
REPORTERS: RAN FANGXU, HE YUANHANG

327
00:27:56,385 --> 00:27:58,065
MENGMENG NO.23

328
00:28:40,025 --> 00:28:40,865
MAIL LOGIN

329
00:28:40,945 --> 00:28:41,825
INCORRECT USERNAME OR PASSWORD

330
00:28:57,585 --> 00:28:59,785
So early, what are you busy with?

331
00:29:01,265 --> 00:29:02,505
Why aren't you at work?

332
00:29:03,425 --> 00:29:06,225
The task force has three days off.
Director Zou approved it.

333
00:29:08,185 --> 00:29:10,465
What's the password for this email?

334
00:29:11,465 --> 00:29:13,185
How did you forget again?

335
00:29:13,265 --> 00:29:15,665
Your full name in pinyin,
plus your birthday.

336
00:29:18,225 --> 00:29:19,465
You haven't used it in years.

337
00:29:19,545 --> 00:29:21,785
Why get trendy now?

338
00:29:26,065 --> 00:29:27,105
INCORRECT USERNAME OR PASSWORD

339
00:29:27,825 --> 00:29:29,145
Still wrong.

340
00:29:30,105 --> 00:29:31,705
Capitalize the first letter.

341
00:29:46,665 --> 00:29:48,345
DU, PHONE RECOVERY

342
00:29:50,345 --> 00:29:53,105
CONTACTS.TXT, TEXTS.TXT, CALL LOG.TXT

343
00:29:56,585 --> 00:29:58,065
CONTACTS.TXT

344
00:29:58,145 --> 00:29:59,585
CONTACT LIST

345
00:29:59,665 --> 00:30:01,665
COUSIN

346
00:30:10,305 --> 00:30:13,785
0535…

347
00:30:13,865 --> 00:30:15,625
32.

348
00:30:23,825 --> 00:30:26,865
<i>Hello. The number you dialed is invalid.</i>

349
00:30:26,945 --> 00:30:28,825
<i>Please check and dial again.</i>

350
00:30:38,505 --> 00:30:39,705
TEXTS

351
00:30:43,505 --> 00:30:44,585
DIRECTOR ZOU: DON'T STAY UP

352
00:30:44,665 --> 00:30:45,745
RAN: DON'T STAY UP TONIGHT

353
00:30:45,825 --> 00:30:46,865
<i>Don't stay up tonight.</i>

354
00:30:47,465 --> 00:30:48,505
<i>Go home and rest early.</i>

355
00:30:49,065 --> 00:30:51,185
<i>I'm fine, senior. I'll leave after work.</i>

356
00:30:51,945 --> 00:30:53,905
<i>That's an order. Go home now.</i>

357
00:30:54,945 --> 00:30:55,785
<i>Copy that.</i>

358
00:30:56,905 --> 00:30:59,945
<i>Ran, I saw a sweater today.</i>
<i>It would look good on you.</i>

359
00:31:00,025 --> 00:31:00,865
SENDER: QIAO

360
00:31:00,945 --> 00:31:02,665
<i>Are you free this weekend?</i>

361
00:31:02,745 --> 00:31:05,305
<i>Sorry, Qiao. I've got to work overtime</i>
<i>this weekend.</i>

362
00:31:05,825 --> 00:31:06,825
<i>Maybe next week.</i>

363
00:31:07,425 --> 00:31:09,465
<i>Let's find a day for dinner.</i>

364
00:31:09,545 --> 00:31:12,225
<i>Okay. Don't overwork yourself.</i>

365
00:31:12,305 --> 00:31:13,705
<i>Get some rest.</i>

366
00:31:13,785 --> 00:31:14,705
<i>Don't worry.</i>

367
00:31:22,705 --> 00:31:24,305
DRAFT, UNSENT MESSAGE TO HE YUANHANG

368
00:31:35,745 --> 00:31:38,385
Dad, what's wrong?

369
00:31:40,425 --> 00:31:41,425
Dad.

370
00:31:55,985 --> 00:31:59,345
DRAFT, UNSENT MESSAGE TO HE YUANHANG

371
00:31:59,425 --> 00:32:04,585
RAN: SIR, THE JUNE 30TH CASE WAS WRONG
ALL WRONG

372
00:32:08,865 --> 00:32:11,225
This message, I never received it.

373
00:32:11,305 --> 00:32:13,625
Ran never sent it to me.

374
00:32:14,985 --> 00:32:16,505
The June 30th case?

375
00:32:17,105 --> 00:32:19,505
Isn't that the Xu father-daughter case?

376
00:32:19,585 --> 00:32:21,385
Wasn't it closed long ago?

377
00:32:22,105 --> 00:32:24,785
Why would Uncle Ran write this?

378
00:32:25,985 --> 00:32:29,065
He must have gone behind my back
to reinvestigate it

379
00:32:29,985 --> 00:32:31,825
and found a major clue.

380
00:32:32,425 --> 00:32:33,385
So major…

381
00:32:34,585 --> 00:32:37,145
it could overturn
all previous conclusions.

382
00:32:40,905 --> 00:32:42,985
Dad. Look.

383
00:32:43,985 --> 00:32:46,745
That was the night
something happened to Uncle Ran.

384
00:32:46,825 --> 00:32:49,705
But this message
was drafted that afternoon.

385
00:32:57,465 --> 00:32:59,425
DRAFT, UNSENT MESSAGE
SAVE AT 2003-01-31 13:09:37

386
00:33:02,025 --> 00:33:03,865
What was he trying to tell me?

387
00:33:04,785 --> 00:33:06,585
Why didn't he send it?

388
00:33:07,865 --> 00:33:10,425
Ran must have left with deep regrets.

389
00:33:12,345 --> 00:33:14,385
Why didn't I see this email sooner?

390
00:33:18,945 --> 00:33:21,025
PHONE RECOVERY BY DU ON JUNE 3RD, 2013

391
00:33:26,345 --> 00:33:28,945
Dad, I brought food back.

392
00:33:29,025 --> 00:33:30,145
Eat it while it's hot.

393
00:33:36,625 --> 00:33:37,745
Dad?

394
00:33:45,705 --> 00:33:46,905
Dad?

395
00:33:48,105 --> 00:33:50,025
Dad! What did you do? Dad!

396
00:33:50,625 --> 00:33:52,825
Don't scare me! Wake up! Dad!

397
00:33:52,905 --> 00:33:55,905
What did you do? Dad!

398
00:33:56,425 --> 00:33:58,625
Don't scare me! Dad!

399
00:33:59,585 --> 00:34:00,425
Dad!

400
00:34:00,505 --> 00:34:01,345
JUNE 3RD, 2013

401
00:34:01,425 --> 00:34:02,265
Dad!

402
00:34:03,545 --> 00:34:04,425
Dad!

403
00:34:04,945 --> 00:34:06,185
PHONE RECOVERY BY DU ON JUNE 3RD, 2013

404
00:34:06,265 --> 00:34:07,465
I get it now.

405
00:34:08,505 --> 00:34:09,344
That time you fainted,

406
00:34:09,425 --> 00:34:10,865
it must've been
because you saw this message.

407
00:34:10,945 --> 00:34:13,225
That's why you kept imagining
Uncle Ran had come back.

408
00:34:16,744 --> 00:34:19,985
So, this is the root of your illness.

409
00:34:23,185 --> 00:34:25,905
I saw this message two years ago?

410
00:34:27,185 --> 00:34:29,705
Dad, think hard again.

411
00:34:30,465 --> 00:34:31,665
After the case was closed,

412
00:34:31,744 --> 00:34:34,625
did Uncle Ran ever mention
the June 30th case again?

413
00:34:40,744 --> 00:34:41,585
Who is it?

414
00:34:43,065 --> 00:34:45,065
Sir, why are you…

415
00:34:48,945 --> 00:34:50,025
What are you doing here?

416
00:34:50,625 --> 00:34:52,784
It's the weekend,
and it's the Winter Solstice.

417
00:34:52,865 --> 00:34:55,625
I brought Qiao to help
warm up your new place.

418
00:34:56,385 --> 00:34:57,225
Ran.

419
00:35:00,025 --> 00:35:01,865
I… I didn't prepare anything.

420
00:35:01,945 --> 00:35:04,225
We're all friends. No need for all that.

421
00:35:05,345 --> 00:35:06,505
Let her in already.

422
00:35:08,265 --> 00:35:09,185
Come in.

423
00:35:09,265 --> 00:35:11,105
The floor is dirty.
No need to change shoes.

424
00:35:16,865 --> 00:35:19,785
Nice place. The bureau treats you well.

425
00:35:20,385 --> 00:35:21,825
Just a bit musty.

426
00:35:22,745 --> 00:35:23,585
It needs more life.

427
00:35:23,665 --> 00:35:26,345
Have people over more. It'll be fine.

428
00:35:26,425 --> 00:35:28,745
I'll get some plants for Ran later on.

429
00:35:29,665 --> 00:35:30,905
Sounds good.

430
00:35:36,225 --> 00:35:37,705
Don't bother.

431
00:35:37,785 --> 00:35:40,345
You rarely come by. Let's eat downstairs.

432
00:35:41,185 --> 00:35:42,705
Why eat at a restaurant?

433
00:35:42,785 --> 00:35:44,905
We're not just warming your home,
we're firing up your kitchen too.

434
00:35:44,985 --> 00:35:46,945
Qiao said she'd cook for you.

435
00:35:47,025 --> 00:35:48,705
How can you refuse?

436
00:36:05,545 --> 00:36:06,745
How nice.

437
00:36:13,225 --> 00:36:15,945
Oh no. I forgot to pick up Xiaohe.

438
00:36:16,825 --> 00:36:17,705
You two eat first.

439
00:36:19,625 --> 00:36:20,785
Sir.

440
00:36:22,225 --> 00:36:23,545
Today is Sunday.

441
00:36:25,465 --> 00:36:26,425
Is it?

442
00:36:27,985 --> 00:36:29,625
Then she definitely
didn't do her homework.

443
00:36:29,705 --> 00:36:31,985
I need to keep an eye on her. You two eat.

444
00:36:33,145 --> 00:36:34,505
Sir!

445
00:36:38,145 --> 00:36:39,545
I'll… see him out.

446
00:36:41,545 --> 00:36:42,385
Sir!

447
00:36:44,145 --> 00:36:46,105
Stay and have a bite with us.

448
00:36:46,185 --> 00:36:47,105
No.

449
00:36:47,185 --> 00:36:50,625
She's already putting herself out there.
You should show some interest too.

450
00:36:50,705 --> 00:36:52,465
Qiao is a good girl.

451
00:36:52,985 --> 00:36:54,385
Don't let her slip away.

452
00:36:59,145 --> 00:36:59,985
Sir,

453
00:37:00,865 --> 00:37:04,105
how's work in the new department?

454
00:37:05,545 --> 00:37:07,865
It's much easier than field duty.

455
00:37:08,545 --> 00:37:09,865
I'm thinking of writing

456
00:37:10,385 --> 00:37:12,665
something about the June 30th case
when I get the time.

457
00:37:12,745 --> 00:37:14,185
A detailed one.

458
00:37:14,265 --> 00:37:16,705
If similar cases come up,
it can be a reference.

459
00:37:18,705 --> 00:37:22,305
Me? All I can do now
is stay in the archives.

460
00:37:23,145 --> 00:37:24,305
I have no choice.

461
00:37:24,385 --> 00:37:27,225
My memory keeps betraying me.

462
00:37:27,785 --> 00:37:33,145
Sir, do you remember the blue heels
from the June 30th case?

463
00:37:33,225 --> 00:37:34,785
Blue heels? What about them?

464
00:37:36,025 --> 00:37:38,025
The bureau had a pipe burst the other day.

465
00:37:38,105 --> 00:37:41,225
Water was everywhere.
We spent ages cleaning up.

466
00:37:41,305 --> 00:37:44,545
But those blue heels just went missing.

467
00:37:47,665 --> 00:37:49,545
Maybe they were cleared out as junk?

468
00:37:49,625 --> 00:37:50,945
But the case is already closed.

469
00:37:51,545 --> 00:37:53,265
Doesn't matter if they're missing.

470
00:37:55,145 --> 00:37:56,145
Alright. That's far enough.

471
00:37:56,225 --> 00:37:58,185
Qiao is still busy upstairs.

472
00:37:58,265 --> 00:38:00,345
Go help her. I'm off.

473
00:38:03,265 --> 00:38:04,465
Take care.

474
00:38:12,065 --> 00:38:13,145
Blue heels.

475
00:38:14,185 --> 00:38:15,465
Ran mentioned the blue heels.

476
00:38:15,545 --> 00:38:17,105
What blue heels?

477
00:38:18,185 --> 00:38:20,705
In the June 30th case evidence,
there was a pair of blue heels.

478
00:38:20,785 --> 00:38:23,065
They were what Xu Meng was wearing
when she went missing.

479
00:38:24,065 --> 00:38:26,505
Those blue heels
were one of the key pieces

480
00:38:26,585 --> 00:38:28,105
of evidence against Wu Shanlong.

481
00:38:28,185 --> 00:38:32,505
Ran mentioned before that
when a pipe burst at the bureau,

482
00:38:32,585 --> 00:38:35,385
he noticed those blue heels were missing.

483
00:38:35,465 --> 00:38:38,585
The shoes went missing.
That doesn't prove anything.

484
00:38:38,665 --> 00:38:40,025
How does it not prove anything?

485
00:38:40,905 --> 00:38:42,145
It means back then,

486
00:38:42,225 --> 00:38:44,305
Ran was already reinvestigating this case.

487
00:38:44,385 --> 00:38:45,465
Otherwise, how would he know

488
00:38:45,545 --> 00:38:47,425
that the evidence box
was missing evidence?

489
00:38:49,305 --> 00:38:51,745
You go to the archives right now

490
00:38:51,825 --> 00:38:53,945
and check the June 30th case files.

491
00:38:54,025 --> 00:38:55,945
See if Ran added any new evidence.

492
00:38:56,705 --> 00:38:57,665
Okay.

493
00:39:05,545 --> 00:39:06,665
Dad,

494
00:39:07,265 --> 00:39:09,425
do we really need to push
this case this far?

495
00:39:11,185 --> 00:39:13,545
These were Uncle Ran's last words.

496
00:39:13,625 --> 00:39:15,265
Do you think we shouldn't push this?

497
00:39:22,905 --> 00:39:25,425
DRAFT, UNSENT MESSAGE TO HE YUANHANG

498
00:39:25,505 --> 00:39:28,385
RAN: SIR, THE JUNE 30TH CASE WAS WRONG
ALL WRONG

499
00:39:52,665 --> 00:39:55,305
WOODCUT KNIFE

